tive_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6] -> v4.0.stable.official [92bee43ad]\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Mint 22.1 Cinnamon, Vulkan 1.3.277 - Forward+ - Using Device #1: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4050 Laptop GPU\n\n### Issue description\n\nI use multi-threading for world building and world loading (chunking). For sometime I have experienced crashes in this logic which becomes increasingly common as I increase the parallelism of execution.\n\nI am grateful that multi-threading has become more stable with each release but I am still seeing a variety of these crashes in 4.4.1. \n\nI have included a text file with a variety of examples of console output during the crashes.\n\n[crash_console_output.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19872094/crash_console_output.txt)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nTo reproduce this simply spin up multiple threads (the more threads, the more common the errors) and add/remove nodes from some node that is not in the scene tree.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nTo reproduce in the MRP, simply playing the scene should cause a variety of crashes, each different for each execution.\n\n[multithreaded_repro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19872159/multithreaded_repro.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/sta